<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Document routes for Matter, Work Assignment, Invoice and Service Request (FR-24)</title>
    <phase>3 BFF features</phase>
    <gate>after 030</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New external routes with SPE access (tags bff-api, auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Tier-2 authorization + app-only SPE access across record types</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file chain on ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs: 030 → 031 → 032</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, spe, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Generalize the existing project document routes (list, download, versions, upload) so the same behaviour works for Matter, Work Assignment, Invoice and Service Request records.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core, Dataverse and SharePoint Embedded developer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Document list/download/versions/upload work for projects, matters, workassignments, invoices and servicerequests under /api/v1/external/{root}/{id}/documents, each Tier-2 checked on the parent (Read for list/download/versions, Create for upload), with the project routes unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Today only projects have document routes: ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:107 list, :117 download (Read on the project + document→project scoping before any SPE read), :193 upload (handler :631, container derived server-side, Create check :655), :206 versions. The to-do routes already generalize over projects/matters/workassignments (:127-:181, RightsForRoot :535) — copy that shape. Document → parent lookups: sprk_document links to project, matter, work assignment and invoice, and to service requests via sprk_relatedservicerequest (live describe 2026-10-10). Service requests are authorized through the submitter scope (the service-requests module accessible set: sprk_requestedby = caller's contact), not the root set. RecordContainerResolver already resolves a container for sprk_servicerequest.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeContainerOwnershipGuard.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDocumentUploadContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRecordDocumentRoutesTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Every SPE read or write in these routes goes through the SpeFileStore facade, app-only, after the parent-record rights check and the document→parent scoping check; SpeContainerOwnershipGuard confirms the container belongs to the parent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Keep the existing /projects/{id}/documents routes and their behaviour; new record types are added by generalizing the handlers, not by copying them per type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The document-row create on upload calls the task-030 stamping method.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external document routes</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the project document handlers and the to-do RightsForRoot pattern.</step>
    <step order="2">Generalize list/download/versions/upload handlers over a root type → (rights source, document lookup column) map: projects→sprk_project, matters→sprk_matter, workassignments→sprk_workassignment, invoices→sprk_invoice, servicerequests→sprk_relatedservicerequest (confirm each column name against src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_Document/Entity.xml).</step>
    <step order="3">Service requests: rights come from the service-requests module accessible set (caller is the requester), giving Read and Create to the requester only.</step>
    <step order="4">Map the new routes in the external group next to the project routes.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per root type: upload then download round-trips (mock SPE); ViewOnly caller upload → 403; record outside the set → 403 on list, download and upload; download of a document belonging to another record → 404/403 (scoping).</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-031-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of the five document→parent lookup columns does not exist on sprk_document, STOP and escalate — do not add a column in this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>If invoices are not in the caller's accessible set as roots (so there is no Tier-2 answer for an invoice id), STOP and escalate with the options.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Project document routes at ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:107,117,193,206.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this task extends those handlers over a root-type map instead of adding parallel endpoints; only the route templates are new.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Users cannot attach or read documents on Matter, Work Assignment, Invoice or Service Request records in the SPA (owner requirement 2026-10-10).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRecordDocumentRoutesTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For each of projects, matters, workassignments, invoices and servicerequests: a Collaborate caller uploads a document and downloads the same bytes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A ViewOnly caller's upload on any of the five types returns 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record outside the caller's accessible set returns 403 for list, download and upload.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A document id that does not belong to the route's record is not downloadable through that route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For a service request, only the requester (sprk_requestedby = caller's contact) can list or upload; anyone else gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing /projects/{id}/documents behaviour and contract tests are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Uploaded document rows carry the task-030 creator stamp.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-24.</notes>

